WEBVTT

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:11.690
After a thousand years, the golden ghost ship has returned to Serenity.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.320
Citizens,

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.200
hear my words.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.580
Good luck, Gruier.

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:20.750
Bentenmaru, full speed ahead!

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:23.040
Set a course for Sea of the Morningstar!

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:24.000
Roger!

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:58.180
A lot happened, but we're almost home, huh?

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:00.760
It seemed long but short at the same time.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:03.430
What will you do with the rest of your spring break?

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:04.600
Hmm...

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:06.850
Go shopping with Mami, work at my part-time job...

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:10.440
Encoded transmission from the Serenity royal family.

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:12.520
From Serenity?

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.900
It's for you.

00:02:16.110 --> 00:02:19.030
"To Kato Marika, Captain of the Bentenmaru:

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:22.370
I imagine you're on your way home now.

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:24.830
I do apologize, but I have another request.

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:29.040
The Serenity royal family is in more danger now than ever.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.920
Please help us.

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:32.420
Gruier Serenity"?

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:33.460
Captain!

00:02:33.460 --> 00:02:35.000
Turn us around, now!

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:35.840
Are we going to jump?

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:37.670
FTL jump.

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:39.930
Set a course for the blue planet of the Serenity system!

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:41.680
Setting course...

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:44.390
Destination: the blue planet of the Serenity system,

00:02:44.390 --> 00:02:45.180
the Blue Sister.

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:47.890
Gruier, I'm coming.

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:57.240
See?

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:58.700
Doesn't it look cuter this way?

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:01.660
Where did you find this ribbon?

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:06.540
It's the debut work from Atelier Mami, Marika!

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:07.950
Atelier Mami?

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:09.330
By Mami, you mean Mami?

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:10.790
Wow, you made it yourself!

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.000
When I saw you on the news,

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:15.460
I said to myself that you were missing something.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:17.550
Oh, that.

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:21.010
I rushed all the way back, and then Gruier...

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:28.980
The captain and crew of the Bentenmaru contributed significant aid to this endeavor.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:34.020
The captain, Kato Marika, will be starting her second year

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:34.310
of high school at Hakuouh Girls' Academy.

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:35.690
A pirate getting a medal from a princess.

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:38.360
located on Sea of the Morningstar, in Tau Ceti.

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:40.450
Talk about romantic...

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:47.410
That's adorable!

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:48.750
That's it.

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:50.000
I knew it. It's just what you needed.

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:55.750
I don't know what it is or what you knew, but I think I like it.

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:58.250
But it's amazing, isn't it?

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:00.260
You're a celebrity now.

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:05.470
Practically no one around here had ever heard of space pirates...

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:07.310
Maybe it'll be good publicity?

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:08.600
What are you talking about?

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.220
You're a local celebrity!

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:13.440
We're going to have to print out tickets for tomorrow's opening ceremony.

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:14.690
What? Why?

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:15.980
You didn't know?

00:04:15.980 --> 00:04:21.490
A lot of the incoming students said they came here because of you.

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:23.200
Huh? What?!

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:27.490
Maybe you should wear this during the yacht club's recruiting drive.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:29.160
You'll attract tons of new members.

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:34.370
Jeez, what was Mami talking about?

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:36.750
Being popular is a good thing.

00:04:36.750 --> 00:04:38.340
It means people like you.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:40.140
Ririka!

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:43.470
Come to think of it, Ririka...

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:45.680
Did you recently change work shifts?

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:46.720
You've been home a lot.

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:49.010
Is it wrong for a mom to be at home?

00:04:49.010 --> 00:04:50.560
No, that isn't it.

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:56.020
But you used to say that it's really busy at the control tower.

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:57.980
Well, you know...

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:01.400
I thought I'd change jobs.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.740
So I took some vacation time while I look for another job.

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:07.780
You can make it on your own now.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:11.910
So I thought I might do something I enjoy too.

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:15.160
Shouldn't I?

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:16.330
You should!

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:19.110
I'm doing what I want!

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:20.460
You should too!

00:05:22.550 --> 00:05:24.000
I see.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:24.920
Thanks.

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:28.140
You really have grown up.

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:30.350
It makes me want to fight even harder!

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:31.010
Fight?

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:32.520
Oh, it's nothing.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:33.810
What time should I wake you up tomorrow?

00:05:34.180 --> 00:05:35.430
Don't worry about it.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:37.310
Starting tomorrow, I'm a second-year student.

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:39.190
I'll get myself up,

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:40.980
so you don't need to wake me.

00:05:41.630 --> 00:05:42.400
Oh, really?

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:43.780
Yup.

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:49.530
I overslept! I overslept!

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:53.490
How could I do this on the first day?!

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:01.950
Excuse me!

00:06:01.950 --> 00:06:02.630
Sorry!

00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:03.920
It's Miss Marika!

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:04.590
She's so wonderful.

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:06.340
Miss Marika!

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:12.180
Excuse me!

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:15.100
Yo, Miss Marika.

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:17.520
You don't have to call me that here.

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:20.270
Wh-What's going on, Gruier?

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:22.520
I don't know what to tell you...

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:26.320
I'm a Hakuoh Academy Senior Middle School student.

00:06:26.320 --> 00:06:28.950
And I'm a member of the yacht club.

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:32.620
What's wrong with a club member being in the club room after school?

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:35.620
But we said goodbye, didn't we?

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:37.080
On Serenity's Blue Planet.

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:39.280
Remember what I said?

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:40.790
"Let's meet again."

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:44.090
Gruier's stay as an visiting student has been extended.

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:46.760
And Grunhilde has also joined.

00:06:46.760 --> 00:06:48.260
That's how it is.

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:54.220
I got jealous when my sister told me how wonderful this place was.

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:57.430
I look forward to studying with you.

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:03.310
Those two are in middle school,

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:05.650
but since they're visiting students from the royal family,

00:07:05.650 --> 00:07:08.070
our club is being asked to look after them.

00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:10.110
Will that be all right?

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:11.910
I dunno why it wouldn't be.

00:07:11.910 --> 00:07:13.990
Syoko and Sasha are pretty grown up.

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:16.330
What? You're leaving it up to them?

00:07:16.330 --> 00:07:19.000
As club president, I'll do what I can.

00:07:19.710 --> 00:07:21.700
More than anything else, it's fun.

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:22.960
Marika's here, as well.

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:27.130
This'll be a fun year for us.

00:07:27.490 --> 00:07:28.880
Take good care of everyone, Lynn.

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:30.630
Yeah.

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:37.350
By the way, how's your recruiting going?

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:40.480
My knitting club's doing okay.

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:43.230
I'm sure you're getting tons of girls wanting to join, right?

00:07:43.510 --> 00:07:46.270
It's the opposite. They're all just watching from a distance.

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:47.610
Why?

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:52.740
People found out that the yacht club can be pretty rough...

00:07:52.740 --> 00:07:54.620
In a way, they're scared of us.

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:57.620
Yeah, all of you do have reputations.

00:07:58.080 --> 00:07:59.620
There's you.

00:07:59.620 --> 00:08:02.040
And then the club president, Lynn, is a famous hacker.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:03.080
And there's a princess.

00:08:03.920 --> 00:08:05.670
And everyone else.

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:08.840
Who knows what they do in their spare time?

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:10.550
I can see someone being intimidated.

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:12.380
That's the problem.

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:14.590
The president says not to worry about it, but...

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:16.640
Then you don't have a choice, do you?

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:19.020
Put on your pirate outfit and go recruiting.

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:20.270
I refuse!

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:23.230
Oh, excuse me!

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:25.310
We're closed for today...

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:30.570
Okay, lock up for me.

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:31.400
Will do.

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:32.240
See you tomorrow.

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:36.870
Sorry for coming by when it's so late.

00:08:36.870 --> 00:08:38.870
No, it's fine.

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:41.200
The manager left for the day.

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:43.000
You look good in that.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:45.500
I've worn this longer than I have my other uniform.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:46.330
Do you really think so?

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:52.050
Well, to me, you'll always be a pira...

00:08:52.050 --> 00:08:53.170
Here you go!

00:08:53.170 --> 00:08:55.220
Marika's special chocolate parfait.

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:59.100
It might not look great, but it still tastes good.

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:00.680
Chiaki likes it too.

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:02.480
Thank you.

00:09:07.570 --> 00:09:08.400
I'm glad.

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:14.650
You really are crazy, Gruier.

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:17.160
You're supposed to be a princess, right?

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:18.700
And yet, you're just wandering around out here.

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:20.410
What if something happened?

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:24.830
I'm sorry, but I wanted to thank you properly.

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:26.040
Thank me?

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:27.960
I'm the one who wanted to thank you.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:29.420
You even gave me a medal.

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:34.340
I can't express my thanks with a medal.

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:37.380
I wanted to talk with you alone.

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:39.430
But that's dangerous.

00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:41.560
You don't know who might be after you.

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:43.890
Isn't it the same for you?

00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:46.640
Well, yeah, but...

00:09:47.260 --> 00:09:49.940
I'm safe by your side.

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:51.980
I believe that.

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:53.320
I guess so.

00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:57.150
There is a non-aggression pact regarding Kato Marika.

00:09:57.490 --> 00:09:59.620
But I don't know who decided on it.

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:07.540
Until that, Serenity was on the brink of war.

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:11.290
Some people wanted a system-wide war of independence.

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:12.710
Some wanted to maintain the royal family.

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:14.300
Some wanted to disband it.

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:19.260
Everything got muddled, and finally they split into conservatives and reformists.

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:24.270
My sister and I thought we were acting on our own,

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:27.730
but we'd foolishly allowed both sides to manipulate us.

00:10:27.990 --> 00:10:29.560
That isn't true!

00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:32.730
You came to the Bentenmaru yourself.

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:37.440
You're the one who saved us, Marika,

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:42.660
by telling us to take the golden ghost ship back to Serenity.

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:44.700
Serenity is about to undergo a vast change.

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:48.000
I just came up with the idea on the spot.

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:53.090
I only thought it would be faster to show them the real thing than try to explain.

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:55.050
I'm jealous of you.

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:03.970
This is the administrator's ID ring I used to disable the Bentenmaru's security.

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:05.770
The administrator's ID?

00:11:05.770 --> 00:11:06.810
Whose?

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:08.680
Your father's.

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:10.230
Captain Kato Gonzaemon.

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:12.980
The captain's ID ring?

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:14.770
I see.

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:17.570
So that's how you got on board.

00:11:18.140 --> 00:11:19.780
I'm sorry about that.

00:11:20.070 --> 00:11:21.700
You're giving this to me?

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:25.080
But my dad gave it to you, right?

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:26.040
Are you sure?

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:29.710
You're the Bentenmaru's captain now.

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:31.830
So I'm returning it to you.

00:11:31.830 --> 00:11:32.750
That's not it...

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:35.170
I want to give it to you.

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:36.090
Please accept it.

00:11:38.890 --> 00:11:40.050
All right.

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:51.130
Hey.

00:11:51.130 --> 00:11:52.230
Yes?

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:54.560
What was my dad like?

00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:58.030
He was a wonderful person.

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:03.490
You are also wonderful, Marika.

00:12:13.310 --> 00:12:15.080
Boy does that bring back memories.

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:16.170
Yeah.

00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:18.420
You've seen this before, right?

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:21.550
Normally, you'd leave that thing in a safe.

00:12:21.550 --> 00:12:25.220
You could use it to control the whole Bentenmaru yourself if you needed to.

00:12:26.300 --> 00:12:27.930
I'd rather avoid that situation.

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:30.270
The Serenity Kingdom has been continually

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:31.270
Serenity's gonna have a unified congress.

00:12:31.270 --> 00:12:33.350
divided into conservative and reform factions.

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:33.690
Each system will receive more self-rule,

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:35.520
And the return of the golden ghost ship is

00:12:35.520 --> 00:12:35.560
believed to be responsible for these events.
Each system will receive more self-rule,

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:37.400
and the royal family's power will be diminished.

00:12:38.650 --> 00:12:44.490
Perhaps seeing their ancestor's ship up close is bringing the whole system to its senses.

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:46.620
I'm sure Gruier is behind it.

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:49.700
If that's true, it's amazing.

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:51.620
Serenity is changing.

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:54.870
That's why Gruier came back here.

00:12:56.300 --> 00:12:57.600
Ririka?

00:12:57.600 --> 00:12:58.380
What?

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:02.010
Can I ask her to come over?

00:13:17.400 --> 00:13:21.690
A big school, with lots of activities.

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:27.360
Just what awaits?

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:29.910
Hi! We're the yacht club.

00:13:29.910 --> 00:13:32.330
We have the famous Miss Marika.

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:36.500
Wait a minute!

00:13:36.500 --> 00:13:38.040
We're the yacht club!

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:39.080
Fire!

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:40.630
Oh, you there!

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:41.960
Want to join the yacht club?

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:42.760
No, thanks!

00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:47.430
Oh, the yacht.

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:49.720
Yayoi Yoshitomi.

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:51.010
I'll do my best.

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:53.060
Natalia Grennorth!

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:54.430
Nice to meet you all!

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:57.020
We got some new members after all.

00:13:57.020 --> 00:14:00.400
I heard she won the middle school solo pilot tournament!

00:14:01.230 --> 00:14:04.010
Uh, I'm Ai Hoshimiya.

00:14:04.010 --> 00:14:05.900
Um, nice to meet you all!

00:14:06.170 --> 00:14:07.990
Hmm... She might work out.

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:10.030
We have an elite few joining this year.

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:11.910
First-year, middle school.

00:14:11.910 --> 00:14:13.740
Grunhilde Serenity.

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:17.580
So we have some new members... Welcome!

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:20.630
We are the outlaws of the yacht club.

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:23.880
Lynn, you're scaring them.

00:14:23.880 --> 00:14:26.970
Well, that's a good starting place.

00:14:26.970 --> 00:14:28.840
They'll get used to it sooner or later.

00:14:29.340 --> 00:14:31.550
But will they ever get used to you?

00:14:31.550 --> 00:14:33.640
Okay, then...

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:37.180
First-years, follow the second-years to the simulator room.

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:40.490
Third-years, we're planning our next practice cruise.

00:14:40.490 --> 00:14:40.940
Right.

00:14:44.110 --> 00:14:45.820
Us too?

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:46.360
Yes.

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:47.150
Gruier.

00:14:47.150 --> 00:14:47.690
Yes?

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:51.910
To your home?

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:53.080
Yeah.

00:14:53.080 --> 00:14:56.830
I'm sure it's nothing compared to your palace,

00:14:56.830 --> 00:15:00.000
but I was thinking we could have dinner at my place.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:00.810
How about it?

00:15:00.810 --> 00:15:02.500
Sure, with pleasure!

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:04.800
Um, you don't have to wear a dress or anything, okay?

00:15:05.380 --> 00:15:07.460
Normal clothes are fine.

00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:09.800
Grunhilde, you should come too.

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:15.640
Ririka?

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:18.310
How are you supposed to cut kombu seaweed?

00:15:18.310 --> 00:15:23.310
It's just for the soup stock, so it doesn't matter how you cut it.

00:15:23.310 --> 00:15:26.860
But if you cut it too thin, it'll be tough to get it out.

00:15:29.130 --> 00:15:30.650
Are you making tsukudani?

00:15:30.650 --> 00:15:31.700
Well, whatever.

00:15:31.700 --> 00:15:33.450
Put it in the pot.

00:15:33.450 --> 00:15:35.030
Keep the heat on low.

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:37.950
Coming!

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:43.960
Come in!

00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:45.540
Thank you for coming.

00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:49.130
You have some pretty serious security.

00:15:49.130 --> 00:15:51.260
Yeah, I guess it's because of my job.

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:52.470
Welcome, Grunhilde.

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:54.430
Hello.

00:15:57.040 --> 00:15:59.180
The captain asked the princesses over for dinner?

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:03.650
She's invited them over for a special Kato family dinner.

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:06.150
Is that really a good idea?

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:08.480
Serenity Squad Commander Catherine...

00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:09.570
Remember her?

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:12.530
The hot one who didn't talk much?

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:16.620
She has a military security force overseeing the house.

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:23.790
And the captain's non-aggression pact should still hold.

00:16:25.500 --> 00:16:29.170
I wonder what food made by Blaster Ririka would taste like.

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:30.010
Is it any good?

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:31.970
An interesting question.

00:16:32.420 --> 00:16:34.930
It was pretty good. Right, Misa?

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:36.930
A long time ago,

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:40.970
when she came aboard this ship...

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:45.150
Her food was so bad, it gives me the shakes just remembering it!

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:46.900
Indeed.

00:16:46.900 --> 00:16:50.280
She almost killed the previous crew several times.

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:52.820
But a while ago...

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:56.700
A while ago, it was delicious.

00:16:56.700 --> 00:16:59.240
It seemed like it was cooked by a different person.

00:16:59.240 --> 00:17:00.990
It actually resembled food.

00:17:02.040 --> 00:17:04.920
I can't believe that she's the same Ririka she once was.

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:07.790
It's time for some piracy!

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:13.350
Indeed...

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:15.840
Maybe she was a different person.

00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:18.890
Not the pirate, Blaster Ririka.

00:17:19.170 --> 00:17:20.890
But the mother,

00:17:20.890 --> 00:17:22.600
Kato Ririka.

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:26.810
She must have worked really hard for her daughter.

00:17:28.020 --> 00:17:29.110
However...

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:31.780
I think it's nearly time.

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:35.530
What's this?

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:36.610
Pot-au-feu.

00:17:36.610 --> 00:17:38.700
Ririka's best dish.

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:40.580
It smells wonderful.

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:41.910
It looks delicious.

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:45.080
No need to flatter me.

00:17:45.080 --> 00:17:46.370
I do think you'll like it though.

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:50.920
It's good.

00:17:50.920 --> 00:17:53.340
Boiled fish-paste, konjac yam, radish, and fish cakes.

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:55.300
Well, let's eat.

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:57.630
Let's eat!

00:17:57.630 --> 00:17:58.090
Let's.

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:09.100
How is it?

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:12.520
It has a strange texture, but it's really good.

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:13.530
Is it?

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:14.820
I'm glad.

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:18.200
Grunhilde! No!

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:26.370
Ririka! Water! Water!

00:18:26.370 --> 00:18:27.540
Are you okay?
Ririka! Water! Water!

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:29.080
No, milk is better!

00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:30.920
Cough it up into my hand.

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:33.050
Grunhilde!
Spit it out and you'll feel better.

00:18:35.090 --> 00:18:37.380
Sorry to make you help.

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:38.630
Not at all.

00:18:38.630 --> 00:18:42.850
I did the cleaning and laundry while I was on the Bentenmaru.

00:18:43.260 --> 00:18:47.890
Marika said that princess or not, since I was on a pirate ship, I had to work.

00:18:48.970 --> 00:18:49.940
Did she?

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:51.690
She told you that?

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:56.650
We were born from the rose spring,

00:18:56.650 --> 00:18:58.880
an artificial womb.

00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:00.660
Yeah, I saw it on the news.

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:05.790
A bloodline created by the correct combination of the correct genes.

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:10.790
We were told that was what the royal family needed.

00:19:11.460 --> 00:19:13.670
And you tried to change that.

00:19:13.670 --> 00:19:16.000
The times are changing.

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:19.510
Not just for myself...

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:24.640
But for everyone in Serenity. We're heading toward the future.

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:29.430
Leaving aside the country, what will <i>you</i> do?

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:34.770
I'm sure you still have your royal obligations.

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:37.440
But as Gruier, what will you do?

00:19:39.950 --> 00:19:42.530
I don't know yet.

00:19:53.320 --> 00:19:54.540
What is that?

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:55.420
I don't know.

00:19:55.420 --> 00:19:58.000
She gave it to me as an apology for feeding me the hot mustard.

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:01.220
Did you have fun?

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:03.640
It was an experience unlike any I've ever had.

00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:06.050
If I stay here,

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:08.680
I'll have lots of different experiences like that, right?

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:10.390
Yes, that's right.

00:20:11.480 --> 00:20:12.850
Kato Marika...

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:19.990
I think I understand now why you like her.

00:20:19.990 --> 00:20:21.030
I see.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.750
That's great!

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:33.790
I'm really embarrassed.

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:39.500
It's a big universe, but I don't think too many people in it have fed hot mustard to princesses.

00:20:39.960 --> 00:20:42.220
I'm glad it didn't become an international incident.

00:20:43.590 --> 00:20:45.470
But I bet you had fun.

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:48.510
Maybe I'll go back to being a nurse.

00:20:48.510 --> 00:20:49.970
Kane, what about you?

00:20:50.390 --> 00:20:51.770
I'll pass.

00:20:51.770 --> 00:20:54.060
I'm done teaching high school girls.

00:20:54.340 --> 00:20:55.650
Oh?

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:58.360
But they all loved you.

00:20:58.360 --> 00:20:59.440
Right, Captain?

00:20:59.440 --> 00:21:03.280
Yeah! I bet the yacht club would welcome you.

00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:04.610
Good grief...

00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:05.660
Lucky.

00:21:05.660 --> 00:21:07.370
You wanna try?

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:08.780
What about you, Schnitzer?

00:21:08.780 --> 00:21:09.870
You could be a gym teacher.

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:11.120
No, thanks.

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:12.700
So what's today's job?

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:14.750
For today...

00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:17.380
It's something the authorities can't really make public,

00:21:17.380 --> 00:21:20.050
but they can't trust a civilian transport with it.

00:21:20.050 --> 00:21:21.920
The usual cargo transport job, I guess.

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:28.180
Research-class electrical components, prototype weapons, medications...

00:21:28.180 --> 00:21:29.640
Huh? A bio-container?

00:21:30.810 --> 00:21:31.890
Cat-monkeys?

00:21:31.890 --> 00:21:32.850
Monkeys?

00:21:33.180 --> 00:21:35.440
Perhaps for some experiment?

00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:38.020
Or maybe for a zoo.

00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:40.440
I know!

00:21:40.440 --> 00:21:43.780
This Sunday, I can take Gruier and Grunhilde to the zoo.

00:21:46.780 --> 00:21:47.530
Okay...

00:21:50.450 --> 00:21:55.250
I can't wait.

00:22:07.930 --> 00:22:10.930
Marika Sends an Invitation

00:22:16.480 --> 00:22:25.690
In the clear night and the silence of time,

00:22:26.570 --> 00:22:35.620
the blue of the pure stars are blended in.

00:22:35.620 --> 00:22:40.750
I'll light the flame of warmth.

00:22:40.750 --> 00:22:45.760
From the flower blooming next to kindness,

00:22:45.760 --> 00:23:01.270
holding onto the impatience and sadness,

00:23:01.270 --> 00:23:11.360
I'll grow up under their bright glow

00:23:11.360 --> 00:23:21.500
chasing after the true sky amongst the stars.

00:23:40.140 --> 00:23:42.020
Everyday life as a pirate.

00:23:42.350 --> 00:23:43.900
Everyday life as a student.

00:23:45.270 --> 00:23:48.750
Kato Marika has traveled between the two in a shuttle,

00:23:48.750 --> 00:23:50.450
but a surprising danger threatens.

00:23:51.280 --> 00:23:53.110
How will she fight back?

00:23:54.490 --> 00:23:56.160
Next time, on <i>Bodacious Space Pirates:</i>

00:23:56.160 --> 00:23:57.790
Marika goes recruiting.

00:23:57.790 --> 00:23:59.040
Look forward to it.

00:23:59.040 --> 00:24:05.040
Marika Goes Recruiting

00:24:05.040 --> 00:24:10.570
I don't know yet.
